{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash32","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff is shell-heavy and depends on Bash 3.2-compatible control flow, sourcing, traps, and strict-mode behavior.","prompt_body":"Investigate Bash portability and strict-mode behavior across the changed shell scripts and embedded release snippets. Pay particular attention to Bash 3.2 compatibility, command-substitution exit-code capture, trap timing, shopt restoration, unset variables under set -u, and sourced-file side effects. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"release-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The release flow now coordinates working-tree upgrade execution, root resolution, machine-readable signals, and Step 8 restart state.","prompt_body":"Review the /release Step 7 and Step 8 integration for state handoff correctness. Check whether root resolution, captured stdout/stderr parsing, release-step7.env writing and reading, fallback behavior, and restart decisions remain coherent across success, failure, and retry paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sparse-cone","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change introduces a shared sparse allowlist library and a critical SCRIPT_ROOT versus PLUGIN_ROOT split.","prompt_body":"Examine the sparse allowlist architecture and all consumers of scripts/lib-sparse-dirs.sh. Verify that the allowlist is sourced from the intended tree, that installed/cache roots are only used for cache and prune context, and that documentation does not reintroduce stale-source ambiguity. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"hook-safety","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"SessionStart hook changes must remain fail-open, non-mutating, cwd-independent, and safe under stripped environments.","prompt_body":"Review the SessionStart sparse-cone drift probe from a hook-safety perspective. Check that failures cannot abort SessionStart, the probe never mutates marketplace state, advisory text avoids leaking dynamic paths or command output, and sourcing does not depend on HOOK_CWD or late-initialized globals. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"cache-prune","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Active-root versus metadata-root selection affects install stamps, cache pruning, and live-session safety.","prompt_body":"Audit cache-root resolution, install-stamp, and prune-protection behavior. Focus on older active roots, newer installed metadata, ambiguous cache directories, same-version cone repair, and whether protected versions can be accidentally pruned or stamped incorrectly. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-env","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The required harness changes rely on careful HOME isolation and re-sourcing order to avoid vacuous or developer-environment-dependent tests.","prompt_body":"Inspect the updated harnesses for hermetic environment setup and meaningful assertions. Verify that HOME is isolated before sourcing upgrade-larch.sh, globals are rebound after re-source where needed, env -i tests still provide required inputs, and sparse-cone assertions are not tautological. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
